{#
/**
 * @file
 * Compact scheme swatch for form radios: the scheme's surface with its default
 * text pairing ("Aa"), three separated dots for the primary / secondary /
 * accent colors, and the scheme's name.
 *
 * Dots show each slot's recognizable brand hue (the scheme-scoped -500 shade)
 * so a scheme reads as "olive / brown / red" at a glance. They are NOT filled
 * from --btn-*-bg-color: those are tuned to stand off the surface, so on
 * colorized schemes they collapse to near-black/near-white and lose the hue.
 * Visibility instead comes from a ring in the surface's own text color
 * (--text-color-default, always legible against the surface), so a dot stays a
 * distinct chip even when its hue happens to match the surface.
 *
 * The name takes its color from the tile rather than setting one: the tile
 * fills with the primary color once selected (`form-item-border` brings that
 * with it), and a name that pinned its own muted gray would be left sitting
 * unreadable on top of the fill. The "Aa" inside the surface is unaffected —
 * that sets its own color, because it has to show the scheme's own pairing.
 *
 * The name is drawn rather than left to a tooltip. Six coloured tiles are not
 * tellable apart by looking, and the element renders as `grid_tiles`, whose
 * label is the whole control — so there is nothing left beside the tile to
 * carry a name. It sits *outside* the tinted surface: inside, it would have to
 * be legible against every scheme's background, and the scheme being chosen is
 * exactly the thing that varies.
 *
 * With no scheme this is the "None" option, which keeps the same silhouette so
 * the row stays even — an unfilled surface and three hollow dots.
 */
#}
{% set dot = 'h-3.5 w-3.5 rounded-full border' %}
{% set ring = 'border-color: rgb(var(--color-base-0-content))' %}
<div class="neo-schemes-swatch flex w-full flex-col items-center gap-1">
  <div class="{{ neo_scheme ? selector }} flex w-full flex-col items-center gap-2 rounded-md border {{ neo_scheme ? 'border-shadow-300 bg-base-0 text-base-0-content' : 'border-base-300 bg-base-0 text-base-400' }} p-2">
    <div class="text-xl leading-none"><span class="font-bold">A</span>a</div>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
      {% if neo_scheme %}
        <span class="{{ dot }}" style="background-color: rgb(var(--color-primary-500)); {{ ring }}"></span>
        <span class="{{ dot }}" style="background-color: rgb(var(--color-secondary-500)); {{ ring }}"></span>
        <span class="{{ dot }}" style="background-color: rgb(var(--color-accent-500)); {{ ring }}"></span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="{{ dot }} border-base-300 bg-base-100"></span>
        <span class="{{ dot }} border-base-300 bg-base-100"></span>
        <span class="{{ dot }} border-base-300 bg-base-100"></span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if label %}
    <span class="w-full text-center text-3xs leading-tight">{{ label }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
